          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The original theorem by Snaith (
            %a{:href => "#Snaith79"}> Snaith 79
            ) identifies the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+K-theory+spectrum"} complex K-theory spectrum
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KU"} KU
            simply as the localization of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-group+%E2%88%9E-ring"} ∞-group ∞-ring
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝕊
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi B
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{S}[B U(1)]
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle+2-group"} circle 2-group
            away from the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bott+element"} Bott element
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi β
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \beta
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi KU
                  %mo ≃
                  %mi 𝕊
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi B
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msup
                    %mi β
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  KU \simeq \mathbb{S}[B U(1)][\beta^{-1}]
                  \\,.
          %p
            Later, further instances of such characterizations of familiar
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/E-%E2%88%9E+rings"} E-∞ rings
            have been given:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                in (
                %a{:href => "#GepnerSnaith08"}> Gepner-Snaith 08
                ) the analogous statement for
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+K-theory"} algebraic K-theory
                is formulated in terms of
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/motivic+spectra"} motivic spectra
            %li
              %p
                in (
                %a{:href => "#Westerland12"}> Westerland 12
                ) the tower of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Morava+E-theories"} Morava E-theories
                (or some
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+fixed+point"} homotopy fixed point
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectra"} spectra
                of these) is shown to be localizations of the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-group+%E2%88%9E-rings"} ∞-group ∞-rings
                of
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi B
                          %mrow
                            %mi n
                            %mo +
                            %mn 1
                        %msub
                          %mi ℤ
                          %mi p
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B^{n+1} \mathbb{Z}_p
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi ℕ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
          %h2#statement Statement
          %h3#preliminaries Preliminaries
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+%E2%88%9E-group"} abelian ∞-group
            write
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                  %mo ≔
                  %mi 𝕊
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo =
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Σ
                    %mo +
                    %mn ∞
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E \coloneqq \mathbb{S}[A] = \Sigma^\infty_+ A
            for its
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-group+E-%E2%88%9E+ring"} ∞-group E-∞ ring
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition Definition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi β
                    %mo ∈
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \beta \in \pi_n(E)
              an element of the
              = succeed "th" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+group"} homotopy group
              %em
                multiplication by
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi β
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \beta
              is a homomorphism
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi β
                      %mo *
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi E
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi Σ
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mi n
                    %mi E
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\beta_\ast
                    \\;\colon\;
                    E
                    \\to
                    \\Sigma^{-n} E
                    \\,.
            %p
              The
              %em localization
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
              at
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi β
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \beta
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+colimit"} homotopy colimit
              over the iterated multiplication with
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi β
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \beta
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi β
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ≔
                    %munder
                      %mi lim
                      %mo →
                    %mrow
                      %mo [
                      %mi E
                      %mover
                        %mo →
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi β
                            %mo *
                      %msup
                        %mi Σ
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mi n
                      %mi E
                      %mover
                        %mo →
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi Σ
                            %mrow
                              %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                              %mi n
                          %msub
                            %mi β
                            %mo *
                      %msup
                        %mi Σ
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mn 2
                          %mi n
                      %mi E
                      %mo →
                      %mi ⋯
                      %mo ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    E[\beta^{-1}]
                    \\coloneqq
                    \\underset{\to}{\lim}
                    \\left[
                    E \stackrel{\beta_\ast}{\to}
                    \\Sigma^{-n}E
                    \\stackrel{\Sigma^{-n} \beta_\ast}{\to}
                    \\Sigma^{-2n} E
                    \\to
                    \\cdots
                    \\right]
            %p
              which has the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+property"} universal property
              that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi μ
                      %mi β
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu_\beta
              becomes an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence"} equivalence
              on
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi E
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %msup
                        %mi β
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E[\beta^{-1}]
          %h3#ForComplexTopologicalKTheory For complex topological K-theory
          %p
            The original formulation of Snaith’s theorem (
            %a{:href => "#Snaith70"}> Snaith 79, theorem 2.12
            , spring) for complex
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+K-theory"} topological K-theory
          %h4#preliminaries_2 Preliminaries
          %p
            Write
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Ho
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Top
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %mo ×
                  %mo ,
                  %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (Ho(Top), \times, \ast)
            for the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+homotopy+category"} classical homotopy category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+category"} symmetric monoidal category
            under forming
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/product+spaces"} product spaces
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+unit"} tensor unit
            the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/point+space"} point space
          %p
            Write
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Ho
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi Top
                    %mrow
                      %mo *
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %mo ∧
                  %mo ,
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (Ho(Top^{\ast/}), \wedge , S^0)
            for the homotopy category of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pointed+topological+spaces"} pointed topological spaces
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product"} tensor product
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smash+product"} smash product
            of pointed spaces and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+unit"} tensor unit
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/0-sphere"} 0-sphere
          %p
            Write
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Ho
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Spectra
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %mo ∧
                  %mo ,
                  %mi 𝕊
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (Ho(Spectra), \wedge, \mathbb{S})
            be the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+homotopy+category"} stable homotopy category
            with its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+smash+product+of+spectra"} symmetric monoidal smash product of spectra
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ∧
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \wedge
            whose
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+unit"} tensor unit
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sphere+spectrum"} sphere spectrum
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝕊
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{S}
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mi B
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi Ho
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Spectra
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A,B \in Ho(Spectra)
            two
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectra"} spectra
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo ≔
                  %msub
                    %mi Hom
                    %mrow
                      %mi Ho
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi Spectra
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi Ab
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  [A,B] \coloneqq Hom_{Ho(Spectra)}(A,B) \in Ab
          %p
            for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom-set"} hom-set
            in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+homotopy+category"} stable homotopy category
            and write
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mi B
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo •
                  %mo ≔
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msup
                    %mi Σ
                    %mo •
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  [A,B]_\bullet \coloneqq [\Sigma^\bullet A, B]
          %p
            for the corresponding
            = succeed "-graded" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℤ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "Introduction+to+Stable+homotopy+theory+--+1-1#GradedAbelianGroupStructureOnHomsInTheHomotopyCategory"} this def.
          %p
            There are two pairs of (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+functor"}> derived
            )
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+functors"} adjoint functors
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Ho
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Spectra
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %munderover
                    %mrow
                    %munder
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi Ω
                          %mn ∞
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟵
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi Σ
                          %mn ∞
                  %mi Ho
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi Top
                    %mrow
                      %mo *
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %munderover
                    %mo ⊥
                    %munder
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mi U
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟵
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %msub
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo +
                  %mi Ho
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Top
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  Ho(Spectra)
                  \\underoverset
                  {\underset{\Omega^\infty}{\longrightarrow}}
                  {\overset{\Sigma^\infty}{\longleftarrow}}
                  {}
                  Ho(Top^{\ast/})
                  \\underoverset
                  {\underset{U}{\longrightarrow}}
                  {\overset{(-)_+}{\longleftarrow}}
                  {\bot}
                  Ho(Top)
          %p
            which are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strong+monoidal+functors"} strong monoidal functors
            (by
            %a{:href => "pointed+object#WedgeAndSmashOfBasePointAdjoinedTopologicalSpaces"} this example
            and
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "Introduction+to+Stable+homotopy+theory+--+1-1#StableHomotopyCategoryIsIndeedStabilizationOfClassicalHomotopyCategory"} this prop
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝕊
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %msup
                    %mi Σ
                    %mn ∞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo +
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathbb{S}[-]
                  \\;\colon
                  \\Sigma^\infty((-)_+)
          %p
            hence takes
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/H-spaces"} H-spaces
            and in particular
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/H-groups"} H-groups
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            to
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ring+spectra"} ring spectra
          %p
            More in detail, an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/H-space"} H-space
            structure is a
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi Ho
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Top
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G \in Ho(Top)
            equipped with morphisms
          %p
