          %h3#for_algebraic_ktheory For algebraic K-theory
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              The analog of this result for the periodic
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+cobordism+spectrum"} algebraic cobordism spectrum
              and
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+K-theory"} algebraic K-theory
              as
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/motivic+spectra"} motivic spectra
              is discussed in (
              %a{:href => "#GepnerSnaith08"}> GepnerSnaith 08
              ).
          %h3#for_smooth_spectra_and_differential_ktheory For smooth spectra and differential K-theory
          %p
            Refinement of the Snaith theorem for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KU"} KU
            to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+spectra"} smooth spectra
            and to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+K-theory"} differential K-theory
            is in (
            %a{:href => "#BunkeNikolausVoelkl13"}> Bunke-Nikolaus-Völkl 13, section 6.3
            ). See at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a{:href => "differential%20cohomology%20diagram#ViaSmoothSnaithTheorem"} differential cohomology diagram – Smooth Snaith K-theory
          %h3#ForMoravaETheory
            Snaith-like theorem for Morava
            = succeed "-theories" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
          %p
            Write
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Γ
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma_n
            for the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Honda+formal+group"} Honda formal group
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/automorphism+group"} automorphism group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Aut
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi Γ
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Aut(\Gamma_n)
            induces for each prime
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            a canonical
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/determinant"} determinant
            morphism
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi det
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝔾
                    %mi n
                  %mo ⟶
                  %msubsup
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mi p
                    %mo ×
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  det \;\colon\; \mathbb{G}_n \longrightarrow \mathbb{Z}_p^\times
          %p
            from the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Morava+stabilizer+group"} Morava stabilizer group
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝔾
                      %mi n
                    %mo ≔
                    %mi Gal
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝔽
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi p
                          %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝔽
                      %mi p
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⋉
                    %mi Aut
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi Γ
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{G}_n \coloneqq Gal(\mathbb{F}_{p^n}/\mathbb{F}_p) \ltimes Aut(\Gamma_n)
          %p Write
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝔾
                    %mi n
                  %mo ≔
                  %mi ker
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi det
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  S \mathbb{G}_n \coloneqq ker(det)
          %p
            for the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/kernel"} kernel
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinity-action"} acts
            on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Morava+E-theory"} Morava E-theory
            spectrum
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_n
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi E
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                      %msub
                        %mi 𝔾
                        %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E^{S\mathbb{G}_n}
            for the corresponding
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+fixed+point"} homotopy fixed point
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectrum"} spectrum
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Westerland12"} Westerland 12, 1.1
          %p
            Write
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi L
                    %mrow
                      %mi K
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mi 𝕊
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msup
                    %mi B
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo +
                      %mn 1
                  %msub
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mi p
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_{K(n)} \mathbb{S}[B^{n+1} \mathbb{Z}_p]
            for the
            = succeed "-localization" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K(n)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-group+%E2%88%9E-ring"} ∞-group ∞-ring
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-group"} (n+1)-group
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi B
                      %mi n
                    %msub
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B^n \mathbb{Z}_p
          .num_theorem
            %h6#theorem_3 Theorem
            %p
              There is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+element"} generalized element
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ρ
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho_n
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/E-%E2%88%9E+ring"} E-∞ ring
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi L
                      %mrow
                        %mi K
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi 𝕊
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi B
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                    %msub
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mi p
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_{K(n)} \mathbb{S}[B^{n+1} \mathbb{Z}_p]
              such that localization at that element yields the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Morava+E-theory"} Morava E-theory
              spectrum
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝔾
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S\mathbb{G}_n
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+fixed+points"} homotopy fixed points
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi L
                      %mrow
                        %mi K
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi 𝕊
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi B
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                    %msub
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mi p
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msubsup
                      %mi ρ
                      %mi n
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mo ≃
                    %msubsup
                      %mi E
                      %mi n
                      %mrow
                        %mi S
                        %msub
                          %mi 𝔾
                          %mi n
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    L_{K(n)} \mathbb{S}[B^{n+1} \mathbb{Z}_p] [\rho_n^{-1}]
                    
                    \\stackrel{\simeq}{\longrightarrow}
                    E_n^{S\mathbb{G}_n}
                    \\,.
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#Westerland12"}> Westerland 12, theorem 1.2
            )
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/splitting+principle"} splitting principle
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+cobordism"} algebraic cobordism
          %h2#references References
          %p The theorem is due to
          %ul
            %li#Snaith79
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Victor+Snaith"}> Victor Snaith
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Algebraic Cobordism and K-theory
          %p with a simpler proof given in
          %ul
            %li#Snaith81
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Victor+Snaith"}> Victor Snaith
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Localized stable homotopy of some classifying spaces
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://www.cambridge.org/core/services/aop-cambridge-core/content/view/S0305004100058205"} pdf
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1017/S0305004100058205"} doi:10.1017/S0305004100058205
          %p using results from
          %ul
            %li#Segal73
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Graeme+Segal"}> Graeme Segal
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em The stable homotopy of complex of projective space
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Segal72.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1093/qmath/24.1.1"} doi:10.1093/qmath/24.1.1
          %p
            Another proof due to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mike+Hopkins"} Mike Hopkins
            is in
          %ul
            %li#HopkinsMathew
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Akhil+Mathew"} Akhil Mathew
              (following
              = succeed ")," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mike+Hopkins"} Mike Hopkins
              %em Snaith’s construction of complex K-theory
              (
              %a{:href => "http://math.uchicago.edu/~amathew/snaith.pdf"}> pdf
              ,
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/MathewSnaithTheorem.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
          %p
            Refinement to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+spectra"} smooth spectra
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+K-theory"} differential K-theory
            is in
          %ul
            %li#BunkeNikolausVoelkl13
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ulrich+Bunke"}> Ulrich Bunke
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thomas+Nikolaus"} Thomas Nikolaus
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+V%C3%B6lkl"} Michael Völkl
              %em Differential cohomology theories as sheaves of spectra
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1311.3188"}> arXiv:1311.3188
              )
          %p
            Discussion of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/E-%E2%88%9E+ring"} E-∞ ring
            structure involved is around theorem 3.1 of
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacob+Lurie"}> Jacob Lurie
              ,
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/A+Survey+of+Elliptic+Cohomology"} A Survey of Elliptic Cohomology
          %p
            A version for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/motivic+spectra"} motivic spectra
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+K-theory"} algebraic K-theory
            is discussed in
          %ul#GepnerSnaith08
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/David+Gepner"}> David Gepner
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Victor+Snaith"} Victor Snaith
              = succeed "," do
                %em On the motivic spectra representing algebraic cobordism and algebraic K-theory
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0712.2817"} arXiv:0712.2817
          %p
            and for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/motivic+cohomology"} motivic cohomology
            in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Markus+Spitzweck"}> Markus Spitzweck
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paul+Arne+%C3%98stv%C3%A6r"} Paul Arne Østvær
              %em The Bott inverted infinite projective space is homotopy algebraic K-theory
              (
              %a{:href => "http://folk.uio.no/paularne/bott.pdf"}> pdf
              )
          %p
            Higher
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chromatic+homotopy+theory"} chromatic
            analogs for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Morava+E-theory"} Morava E-theory
            are discussed in
          %ul
            %li#Westerland12
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Craig+Westerland"}> Craig Westerland
                ,
                %em A higher chromatic analogue of the image of J
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1210.2472"}> arXiv:1210.2472
                )
            %li#LindSatiWesterland16
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Lind"}> John Lind
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hisham+Sati"} Hisham Sati
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Craig+Westerland"} Craig Westerland
                %em A higher categorical analogue of topological T-duality for sphere bundles
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1601.06285"}> arXiv:1601.06285
                )
          %p
            A unifying
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/general+abstract"} general abstract
            perspective is discussed in
          %ul
            %li#Arndt17
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+Arndt"}> Peter Arndt
              , section 3.2 of
              = succeed "," do
                %em Abstract motivic homotopy theory
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://repositorium.ub.uni-osnabrueck.de/handle/urn:nbn:de:gbv:700-2017021015476?mode=full"} web
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://repositorium.ub.uni-osnabrueck.de/bitstream/urn:nbn:de:gbv:700-2017021015476/6/thesis_arndt.pdf"} pdf
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/ArndtAbstractMotivic.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
              %p#Arndth19
                exposition: lecture at
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a{:href => "https://felix-cherubini.de/abstracts.html"} Geometry in Modal HoTT
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=f0wpcNs8hQo"} recording I
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=sTl8637a2Zo"} recording II
          %p
            See also at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spherical+T-duality"} spherical T-duality
